In article <7403@uniol.UUCP> Klaus.Moeller@arbi.informatik.uni-oldenburg.de (Klaus Moeller) writes:
>>DON'T forget the speed boots!  That's "blessed +3 pair of speed boots".
>
>I would never wish for speed boots, most classes have the intrinsic 'fast'
>Archeologist, Elves and Samurais are fast from the beginning, Barbarians,
>Caveman, Knights and Valkyries get fast at the 7th level. Easy to get
>to this level for these classes for an experienced player.
>The other classes get fast when eating a Quantum mechanic.
>Eat them only once, if you're fast and eat one, your speed gets back to
>normal.

The effect of speed boots is MUCH better than the effect of the
"fast" intrinsic.

A character's normal speed is 1.  With the speed boots, the speed is
2.  That means that, against a normal speed monster, you get two moves
for every one move of your opponent.  This means that you can hit your
opponent (or try, anyway), then move one square away.  The monster
will move towards you and not get a chance to swing.  This doesn't
work on certain critters like killer bees, minotaurs, and so on.  Or,
you can elect to stand your ground and effectively double the power of
your weapon.

The "fast" intrinsic gives you a speed somewhat less than 2.  I think
it's 1.3.  This means that you get an extra turn every once in awhile,
but not every turn.  It helps, mind you, but not as much as speed
boots do.

Unfortunately, there is a "feature" in NetHack, such that the messages
in the game do not distinguish between the two speeds.  This means
that when you put on speed boots for the first time, if you are
already "fast," but not "really fast," you get no message about
anything happening.

